WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:04.779
Shopping malls are one of the most common
locations in the United States and are usually

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:06.940
quite predictable and boring.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:12.290
So then why is one mall near Havensbrook,
Indiana one of the most closely guarded SCP

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.750
Foundation sites?

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.660
The SouthWood Park Mall has been shuttered,
with the mall encircled by fencing and all

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.849
entrances closed off.

00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:25.190
Foundation agents under the supervision of
Commander Lana Grey have standing orders that

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:31.419
if anything emerges from the mall, it is to
be contained by any means necessary or eliminated

00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:33.860
with necessary force.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.070
Just what is lurking inside?

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:44.270
This is SCP-4971… a terrifying, uncontained
entity that is capable of initializing a VK-Class

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.940
“Salted Earth” End of Human Habitability
Scenario.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.920
While SCP-4971 appears to be a standard closed
American shopping mall from the outside, what’s

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.600
inside is completely different.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.660
Within the mall is a time-space anomaly, and
anyone who steps inside will find themselves

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.729
in a massive outdoor climate under a sun that
looks to be perpetually setting.

00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:11.270
While the climate and flora in the area appear
to be similar to the Pacific Northwest or

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.899
Yukon territory, testing of samples has been
inconclusive.

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:19.869
What is clear to those who have explored this
biosphere within the mall is that it is much

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:25.640
larger than the confines of the mall and the
limits of its territory are unknown.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.859
But those who wander in are not alone - and
that’s where the threat lies.

00:01:30.859 --> 00:01:37.240
The SouthWood Park Mall had operated since
1985, but by 2006 the last stores closed and

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.819
the mall was left vacant and abandoned.

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:44.049
This sign of urban blight soon attracted trespassers
and criminals.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:48.609
Soon rumors began swirling about the strange
rituals being performed by local teens.

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:53.490
While many people alleged supernatural doings,
no proof was found.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.799
That is, until 2007.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:00.039
It started as a standard break-in, and police
were notified.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:05.340
But as they explored, they started hearing
disturbing sounds - screams and sounds that

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.369
didn’t sound like they came from this world.

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:13.350
The trespassers were nowhere to be found,
despite reports that a huge group was there.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.890
The search eventually revealed the portal
to SCP-4971 - which appears at different places

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.110
in the mall and doesn’t seem to be consistent.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.110
The SCP Foundation was contacted - but several
of the officers who entered the mall were

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.110
never seen again.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.150
The Foundation quickly compiled all the information
they had on the site, and discovered connections

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.110
to a dangerous group.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:33.780
One of the people reported to break in was
Katarina Randolph, a local missing teenager

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:38.720
with ties to Anna Christian, who was a known
occultist in possession of artifacts used

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.590
in summoning rituals.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.020
Both were members of the Daughters of Eden,
a cult that believed that mankind had disrupted

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.260
the natural order and magic must be used to
restore nature to its proper place.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.200
The Foundation believed Christian might have
been in possession of the Last Appeal of Biphi,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:00.189
a text supposedly based on the last words
of a witch killed during a botched exorcism.

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:04.730
Many believed the text had the power to summon
nature spirits to drive away colonists.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.709
While most copies had been destroyed, this
one had made its way from Nazi Germany all

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:13.560
the way to Miskatonic University in Massachusetts.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.349
And now it was potentially in the hands of
dangerous cultists.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.959
While Anna Christian was apprehended months
earlier in a raid on the Daughters of Eden,

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:27.910
the manuscript was nowhere to be found, and
neither was Katarina Randolph - until she

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:33.420
was seen breaking into the SouthWood Park
Mall just before the anomalous activity began.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:38.409
While the book contains several minor rituals,
the final one claims to summon something called

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.719
“The One Who Knows Silence in the Earth”
- the entity Biphi reportedly called out for

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:45.409
in her last words.

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:49.709
A raid on Randlph’s former living quarters
revealed a rambling message where she referred

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:54.799
to herself as a daughter of Gaia and Eden
and vowed to avenge the crimes committed against

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:56.260
Earth and Nature.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:00.379
Knowing these facts, the Foundation debated
on how to contain SCP-4971.

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:06.540
While they didn’t believe the entity had
been summoned, they believed it was in process

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.879
- with the final ritual yet to be completed,
a ritual that requires a high level of human

00:04:11.879 --> 00:04:12.879
sacrifice.

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:16.470
A team was deployed consisting of code-named
agents.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:21.669
There was the team leader Eclipse, fire team
Roman and Mercury, science team Atlantis and

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:24.830
Bangkok, and Nine-Eyes on communications.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:28.700
They entered the closed mall, where there
had been little activity, and turned on their

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.520
lights to see around the darkened facility.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.780
It seemed normal at first, except for the
disrepair and vandalism, but they soon noticed

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.130
something odd.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.830
The mall didn’t smell like an abandoned
building.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.000
There was wind in it, and it smelled deeply
unpleasant.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.090
As they entered the deserted atrium, they
noticed the destruction seemed worse than

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:54.199
expected, with a collapsed skywalk that couldn’t
have been knocked down by the vandals.

00:04:54.199 --> 00:04:58.569
As the team explored an abandoned clothing
store, they encountered a humanoid figure

00:04:58.569 --> 00:05:03.389
that seemed to be covered in thick webbing
- like they had been the victim of giant spiders

00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:05.500
who had planned to eat them later.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.960
And just beyond them, three unidentified figures
lurked but didn’t move, their eyes glowing

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.080
in the darkness.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.490
They left the clothing store, and decided
to watch if the strange figures would follow

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:19.009
them, but they remained where they were.

00:05:19.009 --> 00:05:22.990
The team advanced into the mall, where they
could hear the sound of rushing water get

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.729
louder despite no water in sight.

00:05:25.729 --> 00:05:30.280
And it was clear that the area they were exploring
was far longer than the SouthWood Park Mall

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.330
should be.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.120
A sign on a store seemed to be written in
no language at all.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.509
As the team entered another large atrium,
the mall suddenly ended.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:42.060
And they found themselves in a different world.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:47.270
They stood atop a massive cliff overlooking
a forest that seemed to extend forever.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:51.460
The sun was low in the sky, and didn’t move
no matter how long they waited.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:55.990
The land seemed natural, except for a large
symbol several meters away.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:01.310
It looked like a series of rings surrounding
triangles and smaller rings carved into the

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.310
round.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:06.919
An area in the middle was burned, as if it
had been the site of a fire, and several glass

00:06:06.919 --> 00:06:09.390
vials on the ground had been shattered.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:15.490
But most disturbing was the thick red liquid
filling the trenches surrounding the symbols.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:19.039
A quick analysis of the liquid revealed it
to be human blood.

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:23.861
Further examination of the site revealed an
altar, a machete, and pages from the Last

00:06:23.861 --> 00:06:29.050
Appeal of Biphi - specifically the ones to
summon the entity described in the end.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:34.879
But while the ritual demanded a high level
of human sacrifice, no bodies could be found.

00:06:34.879 --> 00:06:40.259
The ritual was governed by the weight of the
human hearts sacrificed,and an analysis revealed

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:44.830
that the sixty-one people who had entered
the mall and the four officers who went missing

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:48.220
would have reached a sufficient number to
complete the ritual.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.440
The Foundation was preparing to bring in a
heavy fire team to eliminate the entity before

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.950
it became a larger threat, but the team was
skeptical.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:00.500
They hadn’t seen any hostile presence yet
and had no idea what this entity was even

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.170
supposed to resemble.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:06.350
They reported their findings back to Command,
offering to bring back the manuscript and

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.860
other evidence, but were asked to move to
a nearby water source and to hold their position

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.349
until the heavy fire team arrived.

00:07:13.349 --> 00:07:18.259
They hiked through the nearby woods, noticing
an increase in electromagnetic static that

00:07:18.259 --> 00:07:20.289
started to mess with their equipment.

00:07:20.289 --> 00:07:23.730
Mercury soon realized they were being watched.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:28.139
While the other team members were skeptical,
Mercury insisted that five or six entities

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:30.240
were tailing them to the east.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.690
They started hearing odd chattering, unlike
any known animal sound.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:38.879
They couldn’t locate the entity on thermal,
but it soon came into view.

00:07:38.879 --> 00:07:43.710
It appeared to be an animal, but an odd flashing
light appeared around its head and it kept

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.860
appearing and disappearing.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:50.440
As they approached the river, the sun - which
had not moved for hours - suddenly started

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.500
setting, and it became abnormally dark.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:58.160
They tried to make contact with Command, but
the static had shut down their equipment.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.860
All recordings then cut out simultaneously,
and contact with the team was lost.

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:07.610
While the team was not recovered, the Foundation
obtained enough information to put together

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.699
a report on the entity for the Heavy Fire
team.

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:16.690
They had determined that SCP-4971 was the
largest spatial anomaly ever encountered,

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.849
being at least 400,000 meters in volume.

00:08:19.849 --> 00:08:25.009
It seemed to be self-sustaining and maintained
by an entity of enormous power.

00:08:25.009 --> 00:08:29.830
The symbol that appeared in the ritual was
known as the Voxen Eye, and appeared in the

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:33.250
Last Appeal of Biphi as the symbol she carved
into her chest.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.659
It had been referenced repeatedly in arcane
writings and seemed to have its roots in the

00:08:37.659 --> 00:08:39.719
pre-Columbian North American occult.

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:44.910
And it also appeared to be linked to The One
Who Knows Silence in the Earth - the ancient

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.670
being that took its payment in human hearts.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.430
It was time to send in the Heavy Fire team.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:56.649
The team consisted of Team Lead Horizon, Communications
officer Aleppo, and Heavy Fire agents Vestige,

00:08:56.649 --> 00:08:59.820
Kato, Carrier, Ashen, and Wild.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:04.910
They followed the original team, who had lost
contact but was still transmitting their location.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:09.490
The Foundation wanted to set up a long-range
transmitter that would make it easier to communicate

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:12.640
and set up a permanent base inside the anomaly.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:17.990
They advanced into the eerily quiet forest,
the sun back in its usual position.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.120
As they walked, an unknown signal suddenly
came over their broadcast.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.839
It was a song, broken up by static.

00:09:24.839 --> 00:09:26.890
“The Girl from Ipanema”.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:31.540
The team was confused, but they would soon
have much bigger concerns.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:36.560
There was a rustling in the woods, and a large
group of figures emerged, followed by a single,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.339
much larger figure.

00:09:38.339 --> 00:09:44.570
It looked vaguely humanoid, but it was surrounded
by a tangle of branches, vines, and leaves.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.350
More disturbingly, it didn’t have a head.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.529
In place of where its face would be, there
was a strange bright triangle that seemed

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:54.230
to be vibrating in and out of place.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.260
The recorders became more and more distorted
as soon as this being appeared.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.000
The team tried to make contact with the entity,
but it didn’t respond.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.710
They fired their weapons, and the creature
screamed and collapsed against a tree.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.750
The strange symbol shattered.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:14.040
While the entity seemed to be dead, the sensors
picked up a mob of figures moving their way.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:18.370
They heard a high-pitched scream over their
earpieces, and they were surrounded by dozens

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.150
of similar entities.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:25.370
The beings gathered around their fallen member,
the team heard the odd sound of breaking glass

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:31.810
mending, and the creature rose from the ground
and rejoined its brothers - and started advancing

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.230
towards the team.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.800
The team moved away, but was quickly overwhelmed.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.340
Kato fell and was overcome by the creatures.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:41.519
Ashen fell in battle, and Wild lost an arm.

00:10:41.519 --> 00:10:45.030
As the group fled from the creatures, Aleppo’s
communicator went off.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:48.180
It was Eclipse, from the first team, contacting
for help.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:52.930
Horizon made contact and listened to instructions
that told them to head for high ground.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:57.320
The remaining members of the heavy fire team
headed for a nearby rise, still chased by

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.100
the chattering entities.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.899
The ground under them shook, and Wild fell
behind and was snatched by the entities.

00:11:03.899 --> 00:11:08.680
In the end, it was only Aleppo, Vestige, and
Carrier that survived to meet Eclipse.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.670
They compared notes, and Eclipse said they
had been there for a week trying to survive

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.640
against the hostile beings.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.139
But the Heavy Fire team had entered less than
a day after them, and had been there less

00:11:19.139 --> 00:11:20.970
than half a day.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.440
Something was wrong with the passage of time.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.639
But the team had barely any time to reflect
on this in their new safe spot.

00:11:27.639 --> 00:11:32.300
They heard intense static from their radios,
followed by a low droning sound.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:38.079
Their cameras broadcast a single still frame
of something approaching, a multi-legged entity.

00:11:38.079 --> 00:11:42.040
And then their communications cut out and
both teams were lost again.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.290
Additional recordings were found from the
survivors of the first team led by Eclipse,

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:49.470
detailing their experiences within the anomaly.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:53.170
They reported being in there for months, with
their rations running out.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:57.290
While the water was drinkable, they reported
it may be making them sick.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:12:02.910
The plants were inedible, burning their mouths,
and the sun seemed to move only with their

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:03.910
movements.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.610
They approached a mountain, seeking what they
believed was a way back home.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:12.220
But as they approached, they encountered a
mysterious figure that appeared to be a naked

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:16.360
woman dancing near a symbol on the ground
and a human heart.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:21.100
The team tried to contact her, and realized
she was singing the same song they had heard

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.920
on the radio earlier.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.930
It was Katarina Randolph.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:25.959
The missing cultist.

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:29.779
When she turned around, they could see a large
wound on her chest.

00:12:29.779 --> 00:12:34.190
As she ignored the team’s orders, Nine-Eyes
fired and Randolph crumpled to the ground.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:38.100
Suddenly, there was a surge of energy, and
the team was knocked to the ground.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:43.279
A new entity appeared in front of them, a
massive being with a deerlike appearance but

00:12:43.279 --> 00:12:45.529
missing its head and neck.

00:12:45.529 --> 00:12:50.310
Surrounded by glowing orbs and with a massive
white crest in place of its head.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:55.610
Suddenly, Randolph’s body lifted into the
air, and the girl began speaking again.

00:12:55.610 --> 00:13:00.370
She called out to Gaia, claiming the entity
could have her, and Randolph was transformed

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:04.089
into one of the entities as her head collapsed
in on itself.

00:13:04.089 --> 00:13:08.930
The sky darkened, and the team was lifted
into the air, their hearts suddenly pulled

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.550
from their chests.

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:13.300
Only Mercury was left standing, running for
safety.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:21.310
He was cornered by Katrina, pulled his gun,
and the footage cut out one last time.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:25.209
SCP-4971-▽ had been discovered - and it
was one of the most dangerous beings the Foundation

00:13:25.209 --> 00:13:26.540
had ever encountered.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.949
An interview with Anna Christian, now in Foundation
custody, revealed that the creature was sustained

00:13:31.949 --> 00:13:36.110
by rituals - all magical rituals, of any kind.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:41.170
Human sacrifice gave it extra power, but it
derived strength from everything - including

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:45.350
the Foundation’s many magical locks to contain
entities.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:49.779
Stopping all operations would weaken the creature,
but would also endanger the Earth countless

00:13:49.779 --> 00:13:54.160
times over by the potential release of the
other contained entities.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:59.699
It was unkillable, it was near-impossible
to contain, and it was searching for the way

00:13:59.699 --> 00:14:04.790
out into the world - and it was only a matter
of time before it found it.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:09.430
The good news is that there’s a reverse
ritual - but the price is high.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:16.260
The Last Appeal of Biphi contains a reverse-incantation
that seals the portal to SCP-4971.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:21.720
But it requires a human sacrifice as well,
and the cost increases exponentially.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:26.459
The Foundation investigated, and discovered
that the cost would eventually increase to

00:14:26.459 --> 00:14:32.050
the lives of every living being on Earth that
had not already been converted into the beings

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.550
inside SCP-4971.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:40.899
The SCP Foundation was faced with an impossible
choice - here was an incredibly powerful being

00:14:40.899 --> 00:14:46.070
that could end the world, and the only two
ways to stop it both posed an unacceptable

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.389
risk to the world.

00:14:47.389 --> 00:14:52.980
Ther Foundation met to discuss their options,
and came up with a new, esoteric classification

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.810
for this object.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:55.810
Cernunnos.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:15:00.550
Objects classified as Cernunnos can be functionally
contained, but the Foundation cannot achieve

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:04.139
this due to logistical or ethical reasons.

00:15:04.139 --> 00:15:11.690
Therefore, SCP-4971 remains within the SouthWood
Park Mall, guarded by the Foundation, with

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:17.540
SCP-4971-▽ inside and hopefully contained
there - at least for now.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:23.320
For more on unearthly objects contained within
mundane locations, watch “SCP-3008 - Trapped

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.330
in Ikea”, or check out this video instead.

